From: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: let the controller settle after a baud rate change

The controller answers the Update UART Baud Rate command at the old rate
and only then switches. The BCM4354 of an AMPAK AP6356S (Yandex Station)
takes 20 to 30 ms for that and drops whatever arrives at the new rate in
the meantime, then reports a hardware error. The HCI Reset that
btbcm_finalize() sends right after the host has followed is lost that
way and setup fails with -110 at any rate above the initial one; at
115200 nothing is ever switched, which is why it only shows with
max-speed.

Wait 50 ms after the command; this happens once or twice per setup.

Signed-off-by: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -222,6 +222,12 @@
 
 	kfree_skb(skb);
 
+	/*
+	 * The controller switches some time after its Command Complete and
+	 * drops what arrives before: the BCM4354 of an AP6356S needs 20-30 ms.
+	 */
+	msleep(50);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
